    "methodology": "10,000-game solitaire heuristic. Sequencing: land drop, cheapest ramp, commander on affordability, biggest affordable threat, then other proactive spells. Meaningful board = pressure score >= 6 or 2+ threats. Lethal proxy = cumulative combat-pressure proxy >= 40; combat pressure uses mana-value-based creature scoring because card metadata omits power/toughness. Combo lethal = at least one winConditions[] entry tagged kind:'combo' has all pieces present (hand, battlefield, or substitutable) and combined mana cost payable. Substitution priority for missing pieces: (1) bargain free-cast tutor (e.g. Beseech the Mirror) when a non-rock enchantment is on battlefield OR commander has been in play for 1+ turn (approximates Sauron-style amass token from real-game opponent casts); (2) type-matched regular tutor whose tutor_targets includes piece's card type and tutor_mv_cap permits piece's MV; (3) reanimation spell (decklist[].primary_role/secondary_role == 'recursion') for permanent pieces only \u2014 cost replaces piece's cast cost (treats piece as if in graveyard). Each substitute is consumed once per combo line. Tutors, non-permanent combo pieces, and reanimation spells are reserved from filler casting. v2 limitations: no literal graveyard tracking (reanim assumes piece could be in GY), no opponent interaction, no multi-turn assembly tracking, no stack-trigger ordering. Activated draw engines modeled (DEC-472): The One Ring (max 4 activations). Each turn on the battlefield the engine activates once \u2014 its counter total grows by one and that many cards are drawn (the cast-turn draw stays on the immediateDraw path). maxActivations is the stopping rule standing in for The One Ring's upkeep life loss, which the goldfish does not track. Floors: the on-cast protection turn and opponent-dependent draw taxes (Rhystic Study / Mystic Remora class) are not modeled."
